{
  "name": "IT services and MSPs: build a campaign for IT leaders at companies on a given technology",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## IT services and MSPs: build a campaign for IT leaders at companies on a given technology\n\n### How it works\nSell to the teams that run the platform you know best. The form asks for a technology (as Argorant names it, for example a cloud or ERP platform), a country and a company size. Argorant counts IT leaders (department IT, seniority Director, VP or C-level) at companies of that size that use the technology. The workflow saves them as a list and creates a campaign draft with a first email and a follow-up. When the count is within max_people in Settings, the list is added to the draft; above it, nothing is spent and the form tells you to narrow the search.\n\nCosts: count, list and draft are free; adding costs 1 credit per new person.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Set max_people in **Settings**.\n4. Activate and open the production URL of **Market form**.\n5. Review the draft in Argorant, attach mailboxes and launch there or with Campaign > Launch.\n\n### Customization\nEdit the emails in **Create the campaign draft**. Change seniority or departments in the count and list nodes.",
        "height": 687,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "9acc471d-9498-4fee-bc60-2cb2fa536686",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        -360
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Size the market\nFree count and list of IT leaders at companies on the technology.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 700,
        "color": 7
